{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal","id":1529878,"title":"can She-Who-Walks-Alone achiever her goal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-02T21:07:09-08:00","id":1529878,"title":"can She-Who-Walks-Alone achiever her goal","content":"She-Who-Walks-Alone is a A ahroun from the Older Brother tribe in w20 Icons of Rage. and this is one of her plot hooks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Wound the Wyrm: By her own hands, She-Who-WalksAlone lost the only person she\u2019d ever loved. She blames the Wyrm for what happened to Jack, that the insidious force even assaults the hearts of Garou who insisted on violent destruction of a man they\u2019d never known rather than accept love as a greater force of redemption. This understanding partially drives her aloofness from other Garou. She-Who-Walks-Alone knows that the Wyrm cares nothing for its lesser minions, therefore slaughtering them is no true vengeance. Rather than taking potshots at peons for the rest of her days, She-Who-Walks-Alone wants to hurt the Wyrm directly and watch it suffer </div> </div> </div>How can she do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T22:01:11-08:00","id":1529882,"title":"","content":"The first thing that comes to mind is managing to take out a Maeljin. While they are generally replaced, it takes time, and can alter the course of history for the better. Another possible avenue might be to gather together objects, people, or circumstances that are antithetical to a Triatic Wyrm avatar. Just finding out what those might be, or if there even are such sufficiently repellent things for such a being, is a legendary undertaking all itself. Failing that, there's the rite to break the Wyrm out of the Weaver's binding in Apocalypse and put it back together, which would technically cause all of the worst parts of it to cease existing, which would be akin to killing them.<br /> <br /> It's kind of difficult when you get to the top, because &quot;the Wyrm&quot; stopped being a singular entity a long time ago. As a whole, it's spiritually bound in particular ways, cannot perceive of much beyond its own pain, and is basically just thrashing at whatever it detects coming near in a vain hope that this will make the hurting stop. It is kept in this state by all of the Triatic and Urge Wyrms, which as a product of this imprisonment and pain, probably cannot exist without the Wyrm in this state and work to make everything worse so the Wyrm as a whole doesn't snap out of its trance for even a moment and collect itself to get over the problems like some cosmic version of the Human Instrumentality episodes of Evangelion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T04:18:45-08:00","id":1529892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529882#post1529882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing that comes to mind is managing to take out a Maeljin. While they are generally replaced, it takes time, and can alter the course of history for the better. Another possible avenue might be to gather together objects, people, or circumstances that are antithetical to a Triatic Wyrm avatar. Just finding out what those might be, or if there even are such sufficiently repellent things for such a being, is a legendary undertaking all itself. Failing that, there's the rite to break the Wyrm out of the Weaver's binding in Apocalypse and put it back together, which would technically cause all of the worst parts of it to cease existing, which would be akin to killing them.<br /> <br /> It's kind of difficult when you get to the top, because &quot;the Wyrm&quot; stopped being a singular entity a long time ago. As a whole, it's spiritually bound in particular ways, cannot perceive of much beyond its own pain, and is basically just thrashing at whatever it detects coming near in a vain hope that this will make the hurting stop. It is kept in this state by all of the Triatic and Urge Wyrms, which as a product of this imprisonment and pain, probably cannot exist without the Wyrm in this state and work to make everything worse so the Wyrm as a whole doesn't snap out of its trance for even a moment and collect itself to get over the problems like some cosmic version of the Human Instrumentality episodes of Evangelion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Correct if I'm wrong,but of all the Camps,the ones with the best shot of finding a Maeljin and destroying it are the Bane Tenders,right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T05:37:03-08:00","id":1529897,"title":"","content":"I think it's much more likely that she'll wander around, fight after fight accompanied by failures or insignificant victories, and eventually she'll end up falling in Harano and needing to be slaughtered like an animal; Lose her will to fight and just stop everything, and settle in an isolated forest or small town in the middle of the countryside waiting for her days to end; Or being so desperate for everything she had to do and giving up because her revenge that she accepted a deal with the BSD's and agreed to dance the spiral in order to get the &quot;blessing&quot; of amnesia and finally have the peace of just stopping caring.<br /> <br /> Ok, I got off topic, very much off the topic, but I can't explain why, I just look at her story and all I can think is that it's going to have a very tragic ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T06:49:33-08:0