> Inspiring, no, fun, in a very bizarre way, a little. I literally just read this hook and this story formed in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's pretty much the default scenario for failure. It's obvious and likely. Now how do you allow her to matter even in a small way?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T07:41:06-08:00","id":1529904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529897#post1529897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's much more likely that she'll wander around, fight after fight accompanied by failures or insignificant victories, and eventually she'll end up falling in Harano and needing to be slaughtered like an animal; Lose her will to fight and just stop everything, and settle in an isolated forest or small town in the middle of the countryside waiting for her days to end; Or being so desperate for everything she had to do and giving up because her revenge that she accepted a deal with the BSD's and agreed to dance the spiral in order to get the &quot;blessing&quot; of amnesia and finally have the peace of just stopping caring.<br /> <br /> Ok, I got off topic, very much off the topic, but I can't explain why, I just look at her story and all I can think is that it's going to have a very tragic ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were talking about W20, not W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T08:25:15-08:00","id":1529906,"title":"","content":"how old is she again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T08:43:20-08:00","id":1529907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529902#post1529902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. That's pretty much the default scenario for failure. It's obvious and likely. Now how do you allow her to matter even in a small way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on this hook alone, she doesn't seem like the type who would embrace a social or indirect cause, so I think she would look for some larger scale enemy of the Wyrm or secure fetishes, or even hunt BSD's, just the usual basics, I even I thought and started to write a story where I could put her in the middle, but it was going to take a long time and frankly it was getting horrible. The most aspirational (is that the word?) thing I can think of for She-who-walks-alone is as an example of what not to be. Is there anything else you can say about her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T08:52:02-08:00","id":1529909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529904#post1529904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We were talking about W20, not W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was in W5 she would only go to CoF or become a fugitive, I was surprisingly thinking about the old editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T08:55:38-08:00","id":1529910,"title":"","content":"She-Who-Walks-Alone actually an old character, she is from originally the '95 <b>Outcasts: A Players Guide to Pariahs</b><br /> <br /> As for the W20 goal, &quot;She-Who-Walks-Alone wants to hurt the Wyrm directly&quot; it is not actually THAT impossible - of course depending how you interpret the term &quot;hurt&quot;. Sink her claws in its flesh, or otherwise... tho she also wants to &quot;watch it suffer&quot;<br /> The Wyrm is trapped in the Patter Web, the underlying structure of the universe, a manifestation of pure Stasis that binds together different Realms. One of the Apocalyps scenarios is to free the Wyrm from this prison with the help of Queen Ananasa<br /> So in theory, with some Ananasi help She-Who-Walks-Alone potentially could reach the tangled mess where the titanic spirit is trapped. She standing there would be like a speck of dust in contrast of a galaxy, but still, she would be there and could hurt it, as much a <i>halacarid mite</i> could hurt a <i>Perucetus colossus,</i> but still... or just sit down and watch the suffering of the Wyrm that not been able to free himself in the past 360 million years... the sheer volume of the suffering and hopelessness of the Wyrm potentially could satisfy her desire and in a sense she would achieve her goal<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T09:27:16-08:00","id":1529913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529910#post1529910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She-Who-Walks-Alone actually an old character, she is from originally the '95 <b>Outcasts: A Players Guide to Pariahs</b><br /> <br /> As for the W20 goal, &quot;She-Who-Walks-Alone wants to hurt the Wyrm directly&quot; it is not actually THAT impossible - of course depending how you interpret the term &quot;hurt&quot;. Sink her claws in its flesh, or otherwise... tho she also wants to &quot;watch it suffer&quot;<br /> The Wyrm is trapped in the Patter Web, the underlying structure of the universe, a manifestation of pure Stasis that binds together different Realms. One of the Apocalyps scenarios is to free the Wyrm from this prison with the help of Queen Ananasa<br /> So in theory, with some Ananasi help She-Who-Walks-Alone potentially could reach the tangled mess where the titanic spirit is trapped. She standing there would be like a speck of dust in contrast of a galaxy, but still, she would be there and could hurt it, as much a <i>halacarid mite</i> could hurt a <i>Perucetus colossus,</i> but still... or just sit down and watch the suffering of the Wyrm that not been able to free himself in the past 360 million years... the sheer volume of the suffering and hopelessness of the Wyrm potentially could satisfy her desire and in a sense she would achieve her goal<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting,I can't say I know everything about the character but the latter option feels like it might satisfy her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T09:37:03-08:00","id":1529914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529913#post1529913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting,I can't say I know everything about the character but the latter option feels like it might satisfy her</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe<br /> Or if not, she could become the <b>Zhyzhak</b>-equivalent servant/Champion of the Weaver, to make sure the Wyrm not only remain trapped, but reinforcing he Pattern Web and spreading the influence of the Weawer in the Universe, she could make sure, the Wyrm NEVER escapes and as the Web and the Wyrm's prison become so overgrown and calcified, its influence can't reach the world<br /> (A world that probbaly become a Coruscant-like ecumenopolis, or in statis as Luna ended up, but at that point she wouldn't care)<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T10:40:18-08:00","id":1529916,"title":"","content":"Taking the risk of being too saccharine, she could just let go... or decide the best way to hurt the embodiment of suffering the Wyrm became is ti be as kind as possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T12:54:06-08:00","id":1529930,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> But can't really blame her<br /> I mean, bascially every Fera aside the Garou treat Gaia as the spirit of Earth, nature, life, etc, the planet Earth, something... local, and frankly something comprehensible, and the triat are universal forces, Chaos, Order, and Balance between the two via Entropy<br /> The Garou treat them the other way around, thus in their mind the Wyrm is something &quot;small&quot;, below Gaia, their Creator<br /> And this is important! <br /> Because if you follow it/their logic, since Gaia created both of them, they are on the same level, so to speak, so logically, <i>they could fight with it </i>in a huge battle, something they could sink their claws and fangs and claive, something they could hurt and even defeat<br /> Actually the Rokea are spot on in this question, I belive <br /> In their eyes Sea is the source of all, there is no cosmic evil, Qyrl is what she is. Daughter of the Sea who tries to close the &quot;Wound&quot; - the Sun - and wants things back they way they were, dark, cold, something they call the Unmaking, Unsea , the dry land is what the other changer's Gaia is in their eyes. - Qyrl and her sisters exist, she is a Totem even, a very active force in her own right, not somethign enigmatic and unfathomable enemy<br /> <br /> &quot;Unsea realized that Sea's decision to create us \u2014 the race that would survive the Unmaking \u2014 meant that few or none of her children would. With growing horror, she grasped that when the Unmaking occurred, she would be destroyed along with everything except Sea, since Sea was the progenitor of all else. She therefore decided to create races of her own, to prevent the Unmaking. One race, the most (famous among your kind) race of Changers, she created to be her army against the Unmaking. They would fight against the Unmaking as long as they all lived, and they would turn back the tides of destruction. Naive. Foolish. Arrogant. Impossible. The Unmaking can no more be turned back with an army than can a tsunami. But her army was there, nonetheless, and they needed something to fight. And in the absence of some great creature that would bring on the end of all things, they fought the other Changers.&quot;<br /> <br /> And to be fair this is not that far from the truth if you think about it or what happened. Except in a few occasions, there wasn't any great enemy they could marched against (and when they tried, they died en masse , just for irony) Influence, yes, monsters, local problems, powerfull incarna spirits, without a question, but never managed to fight agains the Big Bad itself, the Wyrm<br /> You can't fight with cosmic, fundamental forces of the Universe<br /> <br /> Not to mention, the Bastet are possibly right and the &quot;Wyrm&quot; destructive and corrupting aspect and the Balanced Purifier are two seperate entities<br /> The Bastet say that Cahlash, the original balanced Purifier of the Triat, is still out there, serving his purpose and courting wild Nala (Wyld).<br /> The whole mess with Banes and other nasty things that plague Gaia comes from the Asura, a being that is the incarnated form of Cahlash's hate against his brother Rajah (Weaver) and his despair from his loneliness. When Cahlash ripped the Asura from himself, he hoped that the Asura would destroy the things of Rajah and to fulfill its creator desire, the Asura turned into a multitude of serpents that infested the world, leading to the creation of Banes, fomori, vampires, and other rotten things. All these things may seem to be different, but they all are the Asura in his many faces.<br /> Everything is &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;wyrmish&quot; is an Asura, part of the Asura, who became many. There is no singular Asura entity. Once there was, for a breef time untill it decided to fulfill Cahlash's order to destroy Rajah's creations and became many, cased to be a singular entity. <br /> This actually a bit align with the Garou believes, tho' they wouldn't admit it; Rorg, the Many-Taloned Hunter, is the Incarna of Turog, a destroyed planet that forms the Asteroid Belt, Turog was was destroyed by a Wyrm creature. Not the Wyrm. A Wyrm <i>creature</i>! <br /> No immagine something that is capable to destroy a planet... and not the <i>big bad itself</i><br /> It was a big Asura if you will<br /> Since the universe is working at the monent and not on the brink of destruction, the Wyrm is a cosmic force, not insane and doing its job indeed have some merit<br /> <br /> Then it begs the question: what the hell is what the Weaver trapped in the Pattern Web 360 millon years ago? <br /> If even the Garou belive there are Wyrm creatures that are capable of destroying planets, powerfull and huge enough to do so, it is not really out of the realm of possibility, &quot;there is always a bigger fish&quot; could be applied in this question. <br /> Maybe it is the bigest Asura the universe saw, even maybe the original that is indeed for all tense and propuses is the the Wyrm <br /> <br /> Sorry I digress<br /> Back on topic, in either case, She-Who-Walks-Alone, since she is a Garou and born and grew up as one with the firm belife, they were created to fight against the Wyrm, defend Gaia from it (and in their heart every Garou secretly believes, they one day will face the Wyrm itself and tear it apart) simply couldn't let it go or to be satisfied by destroying only servants and noname banes. <br /> Simply it is against her nature as a Garou<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T13:18:47-08:00","id":1529932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529930#post1529930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed<br /> But can't really blame her<br /