ankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T14:05:45-08:00","id":1529934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529916#post1529916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the risk of being too saccharine, she could just let go... or decide the best way to hurt the embodiment of suffering the Wyrm became is ti be as kind as possible</div> </div> </div> </div>It is mentioned that although Garou normally have the desire to fight for Gaia, exceptions exist, that being said, it is possible that she will lose the desire to fight one day. Now, being as kind as she can is tricky since Garou are afflicted with Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T14:38:25-08:00","id":1529936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529932#post1529932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that sounds fascinating,can you tell me in which books those stories are told? in the bastet and rokea breedbooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>The breedbooks did sing one tune, but by the time the line was ending, that tended to fall by the wayside. In W20, few Fera, if any, bother with trying to fit Gaia lower and positing a radically different spiritual hierarchy; instead, pretty much everything gets made part of the whole. The Wyrm, for example, long since ended up as being a passenger in its own existence beholden to the madness that gave rise to Triatic and Urge Wyrms and their bane servants, which is basically what the Bastet refer to as Asura. The Rokea history was also related by Guards the Shoals, who is not particularly well known as a paragon of tolerance or patience for anyone on land, which might lead to bad takes like assuming that Garou are referring to only the land in reference to Gaia when they've been living by the ocean long enough to know how big it is (the Garou know much more about the world than Guards is giving them credit for, as he tends to conflate every last &quot;Dirtwalker&quot; together).<br /> <br /> Basically, the main beliefs of the Garou are told out of character, whereas a lot of other tales are mentioned by an in-character narrator with various degrees of unreliability - in particular, it takes a keen eye to see where the truth is amidst the stream of consciousness of a Munchmausen Ratkin (other Freak Aspects are only slightly less unhinged), and a capably devious mind to realize that even if the Ananasi seem upfront about their view on the Triat, they're overestimating their chances of infiltrating the other sides' ranks without becoming subsumed by them. The Garou are definitely fuckups, but the Fera aren't exempt from also making some serious mistakes (again, see the Mokole influencing human evolution for tens of millions of years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T17:06:19-08:00","id":1529943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529907#post1529907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on this hook alone, she doesn't seem like the type who would embrace a social or indirect cause, so I think she would look for some larger scale enemy of the Wyrm or secure fetishes, or even hunt BSD's, just the usual basics, I even I thought and started to write a story where I could put her in the middle, but it was going to take a long time and frankly it was getting horrible. The most aspirational (is that the word?) thing I can think of for She-who-walks-alone is as an example of what not to be. Is there anything else you can say about her?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that your scenario is a bummer. Nicolas came in looking for ways for her to hurt the Wyrm, not for ways for her to fail miserably. So provide those instead of delving into how bad things can go. Nothing stops us from going big and imaginative here:<ul><li>taking the perfect metis under her own wing and brining it up as a kind protector that rejects the Wyrm</li> <li>founding an organisation that explores the Maeljin and provides systemic tools to identify and destroy them all</li> <li>selling her soul to the Weaver to finally imprison the Wyrm once and for all</li> <li>finding a gift or item that reliably and safely cures fomori or fixes banes</li> </ul>Dream big.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529934#post1529934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is mentioned that although Garou normally have the desire to fight for Gaia, exceptions exist, that being said, it is possible that she will lose the desire to fight one day. Now, being as kind as she can is tricky since Garou are afflicted with Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou can be quite kind. Their character is not defined by Rage, their propensity to flip out over certain stimuli and having to practice how to keep self control make their lives more difficult, but doesn't mean they lack empathy, kindeness or desire to do good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T04:14:49-08:00","id":1529968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529943#post1529943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm saying that your scenario is a bummer. Nicolas came in looking for ways for her to hurt the Wyrm, not for ways for her to fail miserably. So provide those instead of delving into how bad things can go. Nothing stops us from going big and imaginative here:<ul><li>taking the perfect metis under her own wing and brining it up as a kind protector that rejects the Wyrm</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>As much as I love the idea of a discredited veteran finding hope in a child he develops a family bond with, and as much as I think it's a good hook, I really don't think it's a case of a Garou with a thirst for revenge. Why wouldn't she just kill the child?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529943#post1529943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">founding an organisation that explores the Maeljin and provides systemic tools to identify and destroy them all</div> </div> </div> </div></li> </ul><br /> This idea was good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529943#post1529943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">selling her soul to the Weaver to finally imprison the Wyrm once and for all</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a good one, I wish I had thought of that, it's almost like going BSD, but aimed at Weaver, if I understand correctly. By the way, that wasn't sarcasm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529943#post1529943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">finding a gift or item that reliably and safely cures fomori or fixes banes</div> </div> </div> </div>It even works, I just think that an item or skill capable of doing this so conveniently is, and I apologize for what I'm about to say, just boring (That's not really the word I wanted, but it doesn't have an English translation.) , plus if the Wyrm doesn't care about it's minions, then what difference does it make to it if they are healed instead of killed, better yet, if they are still alive what stops them from being transformed again? Isn't better for the wyrm like that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529943#post1529943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dream big.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't dream big, I become megalomaniac and that doesn't end well for anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529878-can-she-who-walks-alone-achiever-her-goal?p=1529943#post1529943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou can be quite kind. Their character is not defined by Rage, their propensity to flip out over certain stimuli and having to practice how to keep self control make their lives more difficult, but doesn't mean they lack empathy, kindeness or desire to do good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just said it was complicated.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T04:17:23-08:00","id":1530016,"title":"","content":"My own instinctive response is that, this being WEREWOLF, the character can definately land a blow on the Wyrm itself - especially with the help of local PCs, but that it\u2019s going to take more than just one adventure to set up the circumstances in which she can do so and there\u2019s every likelihood that this is a suicide mission.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also very likely that success in this mission will make the character a Legend, but that it will be a personal triumph, rather than a Major Victory in the Apocalypse War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}